  "claimBoundary": "This validates one exact-content local checkpoint helper run on a working tree based on revision f73bc24 after a fresh build. The helper and its imported build artifacts are hash-bound; its raw result is bound by byte count and SHA-256. It bound the public E1 specification, clean fixture baseline and unchanged non-checkpoint paths, module dependency, exact changed paths, core tests, persisted Codex process identity, and a renewed controller lease before signaling that runtime. The Mission then completed one real Codex-to-Qoder handoff and both the original verification and an explicit reverification produced verified Receipts. The target workspace digest matched the source checkpoint when acknowledgement was observed; this does not prove that the target runtime performed no transient action before acknowledgement. This is not controller-crash recovery, a clean-clone validation of a published helper revision, third-party or cross-host reproduction, production readiness, broad runtime compatibility, or evidence of guarded or enforced Effect deduplication."
